<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Mbappe apologizes as Chinese sponsors drop him and TV broadcasts are halted over Mao dictator remark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:deb0d7f427e06acb8b849dae4037a3a82357cf908fe03f35659ceb76cbe483bb</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831--140a68dc18a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French soccer star Kylian Mbappe has apologized after apparently referring to Mao Zedong as a dictator. Chinese sponsors have dropped him, while state television has suspended Spanish league broadcasts.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Is the US undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9113a8cf9acd66e50daaffd967ea8fdd5fa7ae2acbf5f1d61677df8b26f35c91</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863--db2dea3e5776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With the US reopening talks with Myanmar's military-backed government, and several Southeast Asian countries restarting diplomatic contacts, the EU is facing uncomfortable questions about its own boycott of the junta.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e62592511b46894eb26c331111da9f059d08e18d792f188df6932faa2edbf0f</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Arunachal sees fresh violence over proposed dam</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a26ab38374674b7bc4f9734dc248ce557d0a277ea90ed19e11cacc71eb598b48</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650--d59bfea6f557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More violence erupted in India's northeastern state of Arunachal Pradesh over proposed hydroelectric projects that locals are protesting. Also, India's top court will hear pleas against the poll body chief.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz in Asia as security issues loom large</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60042dbe11d260b66f89bb8d58df4bae3d4bd13a2d863c7638844bc169a63bc9</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-in-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065--009b584587c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-in-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz will be meeting the leaders of Singapore, Japan and South Korea as Germany seeks to adjust its foreign policy to rising uncertainty and threats to global supply chains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Steinmeier in China: A major state visit in uncertain times</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1eda7986ab9105c9e2651c1b396630cb9ac31bedca86bee86cf0152b67562995</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205--23bd9ee47a5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Frank-Walter Steinmeier is traveling to China on a state visit in a period of political and economic uncertainty. Germany is seeking alternative partners in the region but also wants good ties with Beijing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Remark on Modi's father stirs political row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76b3b01106bb258890bca38a2be4426960451dd63381c0ff481ef9677de2c13c</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-remark-on-modi-s-father-stirs-political-row/live-79758965--7e6cacdc5195.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-remark-on-modi-s-father-stirs-political-row/live-79758965?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An opposition leader's impromptu remark concerning PM Modi is causing a political stir in India with the ruling party now planning a protest. Also, the prince of Liechtenstein is in Mumbai.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a9c40dd754703cd229bef7547028e2825ba7893d4758eaa415a4ea4bd45cd7</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a6a61174d241e9be2370cee6bcba64de1ea54653965ea96e3c4c51802b9b54</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
